---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/PageHead.astro';
---
<Base title="Taking part">
  <PageHead eyebrow="Learn" title="Taking part" lead="You have a legal right to a say in how the county is run. Here are four ways to use it." crumbs={[{ href: '/learn/', label: 'Learn' }, { href: '/learn/taking-part/', label: 'Taking part' }]} />
  <div class="stack-lg" style="margin-top:16px; max-width:760px">
    <p class="callout"><span>Ready to write? Use the <a href="/take-part/submission/">submission helper</a> for a forum, plan or petition, or <a href="/ask/">Ask Nyamira</a> for an information request.</span></p>
    <section class="stack">
      <h2>1. Speak at a public forum</h2>
      <p>The county must hold public forums before it approves its budget and plans. Notices are posted on the county website, in newspapers, on radio and through ward administrators. Go with one clear point, for example: "The dispensary in our village has no maternity room. Please fund one in next year's budget."</p>
      <p class="small muted">Why you can: Constitution Articles 174, 196 and 201; County Governments Act, 2012 (Part VIII, citizen participation); Public Finance Management Act, 2012, section 125.</p>
      <p>The budget forums usually come between September and February. See the <a href="/learn/budget-calendar/">budget calendar</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="stack">
      <h2>2. Attend an Assembly sitting</h2>
      <p>County Assembly sittings and committee meetings are open to the public. You can watch from the public gallery, and committees often invite comments on bills.</p>
      <p class="small muted">Why you can: Constitution Article 196.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="stack">
      <h2>3. Petition the County Assembly</h2>
      <p>Anyone can petition the Assembly to act on a county matter: to pass, change or repeal a law, or to look into a problem. Write the petition clearly, say what you want the Assembly to do, sign it, and deliver it to the Clerk of the County Assembly. Your MCA can help present it.</p>
      <p class="small muted">Why you can: Petitions to County Assemblies (Procedure) Act, 2013.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="stack">
      <h2>4. Ask for information</h2>
      <p>You can ask the county for information it holds, such as a contract, a project's budget or a tender result. Write to the county's information access officer and keep a copy. The law sets a deadline for a reply (generally 21 days). If you are refused, you can complain to the Commission on Administrative Justice (the Ombudsman).</p>
      <p class="small muted">Why you can: Constitution Article 35; Access to Information Act, 2016.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="sw" lang="sw">
      <span class="eyebrow">Muhtasari kwa Kiswahili</span>
      <p>Una haki ya kushiriki katika uongozi wa kaunti: kuhudhuria mikutano ya umma kuhusu bajeti, kuhudhuria vikao vya Bunge la Kaunti, kuwasilisha ombi (petition) kwa Bunge, na kuomba habari kutoka kwa kaunti.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
